  "description": "Change of use of part of the ground floor commercial unit from office use to flexible use within Class E.",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\n\r\nLocation plan, 26/001/01, 26/001/02, 26/001/03, cover letter dated 27 February 2026, Planning Statement dated 27 February 2026. \r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - Should the unit be used for restaurant/caf� use (Class E (a) and (b)), the use shall not be carried out outside the following times 07:00 to 23:30 Sunday to Thursday and Bank Holidays; and 07:00 to 00:30 on Friday and Saturday. \r\n \r\nReason: To safeguard the amenities of the adjoining premises and the area generally in accordance with the requirements of policies A1 (Managing the impact of development), A4 (Noise and vibration) and TC4 (Town centre uses) of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - No music emanating from the unit shall be audible within any adjoining premises between 2100 hrs and 0800 hrs. \r\n \r\nReason: To safeguard the amenities of the adjoining premises and the area generally in accordance with the requirements of policies A1 (Managing the impact of development) and A4 (Noise and vibration) of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The external noise level emitted from plant, machinery or equipment at the development hereby approved shall be lower than the typical existing background noise level by at least 10dBA, or by 15dBA where the source is tonal, as assessed according to BS4142:2014 at the nearest and/or most affected noise sensitive premises, with all machinery operating together at maximum capacity.\r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the amenities of the adjoining premises and the area generally in accordance with the requirements of policies A1 and A4 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
